WEBVTT

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.298
The prey's course
has become erratic.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.311
I will intercept to kill.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.312
No.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.439
Maintain distance.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.916
His ship is damaged.

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.578
He's injured.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.109
Let him bleed.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:23.452
This prey is resilient.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.720
We will lose the moment.

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:30.688
The way a creature behaves
when it is wounded

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.324
is the key to its destruction.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.561
Maintain distance.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:39.839
Direct hit.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:42.000
Our hull armor is stable.

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:44.873
His weapons must be weakening.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:48.506
The prey is heading
for an asteroid belt.

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:51.483
Vector 168.9.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.824
We are losing him.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:02.294
He hasn't come here to hide.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:06.264
He's come to make a final stand.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.162
Tracking.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:17.342
He's holding position
above an asteroid

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.504
and he's left his ship.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:21.207
Follow him.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:06.085
The prey is scattering
our sensors.

00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:08.356
Impressive.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:12.160
He counters our pursuit
to the final moment.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.825
Compensating.

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:17.325
No. Disengage sensors.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.962
For what reason?

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:22.940
I want to take him
with my own eyes.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:24.603
Follow.

00:02:34.554 --> 00:02:36.613
I'll draw his attack.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:39.216
Prepare to target
his thoracic crest.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.840
A flawless kill.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.757
"Please remain still so that
I can treat your injuries.

00:05:30.796 --> 00:05:32.286
"Thank you.

00:05:32.331 --> 00:05:34.561
"I'm sorry. Did that hurt?

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.625
"I'll try to be more careful.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:39.638
"Thanks for being
a patient patient.

00:05:39.672 --> 00:05:41.970
Have a pleasant afternoon."
This is absurd.

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.303
Not at all.
Keep going.

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:44.468
You're doing fine.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:45.977
This vernacular
is not applicable

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:47.137
to my duties on Voyager.

00:05:47.179 --> 00:05:48.612
We can tailor the vocabulary

00:05:48.647 --> 00:05:51.081
to your specific situations
a little later.

00:05:51.116 --> 00:05:53.277
Right now, it's the sentiment
that counts.

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:55.150
I don't see the relevance.

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:57.587
I created these exercises
three years ago

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:00.114
to familiarize myself
with the social graces.

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:03.026
I found that if I repeated
them several times each day,

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.462
the words became
almost second nature.

00:06:05.497 --> 00:06:07.124
Let's continue.

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:09.930
Exercise two:
"The workplace encounter."

00:06:10.035 --> 00:06:11.866
Kes used to help me
with this one.

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.371
Now I'll be the nurse.
You be the doctor.

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:19.936
"Please hand me the hypospray."

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.877
"Of course, Doctor,
immediately."

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.848
"Thank you.
Looks at instrument."

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:26.408
No, no. Don't read that part...
only the dialogue.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:30.283
"Excuse me, Nurse.

00:06:30.322 --> 00:06:32.153
"This is the wrong hypospray.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.056
Would you mind finding
the correct one?"

00:06:34.093 --> 00:06:35.253
"Not at all."

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:36.283
"Thank you."

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:38.523
"Did I mention you
look lovely today?"

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:39.963
"Oh, Doctor,
you're so charming."

00:06:40.065 --> 00:06:42.693
This lesson is terminated.

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:46.605
I know it's awkward.

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:48.106
For me, it was even painful,

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:50.574
but I think you'll find the
rewards well worth the effort.

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:52.133
Rewards.

00:06:52.177 --> 00:06:54.737
The ability
to put others at ease...

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.374
make them feel
more comfortable around you.

00:06:57.416 --> 00:07:00.317
You're a lot like me
when I was first activated.

00:07:00.352 --> 00:07:01.580
If I'd had a mentor,

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:04.418
things would have gone
a lot more smoothly.

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:07.186
I'm willing to share my wisdom,

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:11.162
but, if you're not interested...
fine.

00:07:11.196 --> 00:07:13.391
I'll stick to your
physiological maintenance.

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:17.232
I will examine your data.

00:07:17.269 --> 00:07:18.827
Oh, good.

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:21.237
Pay special attention
to Exercise 17:

00:07:21.273 --> 00:07:23.002
"Bridge banter for beginners."

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:30.876
Have a pleasant day.

00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:33.646
Hmm?

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:35.085
Verify.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:36.348
Monotanium hull plating,

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:38.481
dicyclic warp signature...

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:40.549
the vessel is definitely
Hirogen.

00:07:40.592 --> 00:07:41.889
They're moving to intercept.

00:07:41.927 --> 00:07:42.951
Evasive maneuvers?

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:45.758
No. We need to settle
our differences here and now.

00:07:45.798 --> 00:07:47.265
Hard about, full impulse.

00:07:47.299 --> 00:07:49.267
Red Alert.

00:07:49.301 --> 00:07:50.893
They're in visual range.

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:53.063
On screen.

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:54.595
Hail them.

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:57.666
No response.

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:58.768
They're closing.

00:07:58.811 --> 00:08:01.439
50,000 kilometers...

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:04.608
forty-five... forty...

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.413
Maintain course, Mr. Paris.

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:07.851
Curious.

00:08:07.886 --> 00:08:10.218
They are not charging weapons.

00:08:10.255 --> 00:08:11.916
They're slowing, sir.

00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:13.049
Life signs?

00:08:13.092 --> 00:08:14.081
Only one.

00:08:14.126 --> 00:08:15.491
And it's erratic.

00:08:15.527 --> 00:08:17.358
They've stopped, Captain.

00:08:17.396 --> 00:08:19.364
Their engines
just went off-line.

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:22.893
This could be a trap.

00:08:22.935 --> 00:08:26.393
Harry, run a long-range scan.

00:08:26.438 --> 00:08:28.770
Are there any other
Hirogen ships out there?

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:33.577
None.

00:08:36.081 --> 00:08:38.276
Take us
within transporter range.

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.615
You intend to board their ship.

00:08:40.652 --> 00:08:41.619
Yes.

00:08:41.653 --> 00:08:44.554
The Hirogen vessel is
a potential threat.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:46.421
We should destroy it.

00:08:46.458 --> 00:08:50.394
Seven, what you call a threat,
I call an opportunity...

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:52.761
to gain knowledge
about this species...

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:56.131
and in this case,
maybe even show some compassion.

00:08:56.168 --> 00:08:59.296
There seems to be
a wounded pilot over there.

00:08:59.338 --> 00:09:01.135
Our experience
with the Hirogen indicates

00:09:01.173 --> 00:09:03.641
that compassion
would not be reciprocated.

00:09:03.675 --> 00:09:05.768
And all of my experience says

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.972
we've got to take
that chance anyway.

00:09:10.249 --> 00:09:12.513
Commander.

00:09:12.551 --> 00:09:14.178
Tuvok, Paris, you're with me.

00:09:42.681 --> 00:09:44.376
Looks like there was a fight.

00:09:46.985 --> 00:09:48.885
Search for the life signs.

00:10:37.936 --> 00:10:39.631
Commander.

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:43.999
I'm reading bones,
muscle tissue...

00:10:44.042 --> 00:10:45.976
from at least
nine different species.

00:10:46.011 --> 00:10:49.174
It's all being broken down
by some sort of enzyme.

00:10:49.214 --> 00:10:53.014
Perhaps this is their method
of denaturating their prey.

00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:56.680
Either that... or it's dinner.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.105
Looks like somebody
lost their helmet.

00:11:34.927 --> 00:11:36.451
Commander.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.926
I'm not picking up
any weapon residuals.

00:11:40.966 --> 00:11:43.901
I'd say he was
physically torn apart.

00:11:46.371 --> 00:11:47.998
I'm picking up the life signs.

00:11:48.073 --> 00:11:49.062
This way.

00:12:12.598 --> 00:12:14.156
Massive internal bleeding.

00:12:14.199 --> 00:12:15.928
Let's get him to Sick Bay.

00:12:19.471 --> 00:12:21.735
The data we downloaded
from the ship's computer

00:12:21.773 --> 00:12:23.240
included navigational records.

00:12:23.275 --> 00:12:25.106
Can you give us a map
of this region?

00:12:27.913 --> 00:12:30.143
This is the Hirogen vessel's
flight path

00:12:30.182 --> 00:12:31.615
over the past five years.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:34.278
They've certainly covered
a lot of space.

00:12:34.319 --> 00:12:35.343
This ship alone has visited

00:12:35.387 --> 00:12:37.548
over 90 star systems
in the last year.

00:12:37.589 --> 00:12:39.250
I analyzed some of their logs.

00:12:39.291 --> 00:12:41.282
From what I can tell,
this is a hunting species.

00:12:41.326 --> 00:12:43.851
We saw the skeletal remains

00:12:43.895 --> 00:12:47.092
from dozens of alien races
displayed like trophies.

00:12:47.132 --> 00:12:48.258
There was also evidence

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.393
they may be using some
of their victims for food.

00:12:50.435 --> 00:12:53.529
The entire culture
seems to be based on the hunt...

00:12:53.572 --> 00:12:55.870
social rituals, art,
religious beliefs.

00:12:55.907 --> 00:12:57.306
They're nomadic.

00:12:57.342 --> 00:12:59.503
Their existence is driven
by the pursuit of prey.

00:12:59.544 --> 00:13:01.705
And it's carried them
across huge distances.

00:13:01.747 --> 00:13:03.806
There is no evidence
of a home planet.

00:13:03.849 --> 00:13:06.909
Their ships travel alone
or in small groups.

00:13:06.952 --> 00:13:09.147
On occasion,
several will join forces

00:13:09.187 --> 00:13:10.620
in a multipronged attack.

00:13:10.656 --> 00:13:12.283
Like wolves.

00:13:14.026 --> 00:13:15.857
How's our "wolf" in Sick Bay?

00:13:15.894 --> 00:13:19.125
Still unconscious...
behind a level-5 force field.

00:13:20.732 --> 00:13:22.597
You were right, Seven.

00:13:22.634 --> 00:13:24.226
This species is a threat.

00:13:24.269 --> 00:13:26.499
But despite the risk
of sending an away team,

00:13:26.538 --> 00:13:29.439
we know a lot more about
who we're dealing with now.

00:13:29.474 --> 00:13:31.203
You were correct, Captain.

00:13:31.243 --> 00:13:32.904
It was worth the risk...

00:13:32.944 --> 00:13:34.309
this time.

00:13:37.916 --> 00:13:40.851
So, there's
one question remaining.

00:13:40.886 --> 00:13:43.980
Who's hunting the hunters?

00:13:59.471 --> 00:14:01.462
I was trying to remove
his body armor

00:14:01.506 --> 00:14:03.406
to treat the internal injuries,

00:14:03.442 --> 00:14:05.273
when he suddenly
regained consciousness.

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:07.870
Needless to say,
he's not happy to be here.

00:14:07.913 --> 00:14:08.937
Can you sedate him?

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:09.947
I've already tried.

00:14:09.981 --> 00:14:11.949
His immune system
neutralizes everything.

00:14:11.983 --> 00:14:13.917
I could synthesize
a more potent compound,

00:14:13.952 --> 00:14:15.146
but that would take hours.

00:14:15.187 --> 00:14:16.484
He could be dead by then.

00:14:16.521 --> 00:14:18.011
His wounds are severe.

00:14:20.459 --> 00:14:22.859
Your crewmate is dead...

00:14:22.894 --> 00:14:26.557
and your ship has been damaged
beyond repair.

00:14:26.598 --> 00:14:29.123
I brought you here
to treat your injuries.

00:14:29.167 --> 00:14:32.102
What happened to your ship?

00:14:32.137 --> 00:14:34.196
Who attacked you?

00:14:37.109 --> 00:14:38.542
The first time
I met your species,

00:14:38.577 --> 00:14:41.546
it wasn't on the best of terms,
but that doesn't mean you and I

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:44.140
can't find a way to change that.

00:14:44.182 --> 00:14:45.444
Our prey.

00:14:45.484 --> 00:14:47.952
You were on a hunt.

00:14:47.986 --> 00:14:49.886
Yes.

00:14:49.921 --> 00:14:51.912
A formidable alien.

00:14:51.957 --> 00:14:54.152
We captured it two days ago,

00:14:54.192 --> 00:14:55.625
but it broke free

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.322
of its restraints...
attacked us.

00:14:58.363 --> 00:14:59.796
Release me.

00:14:59.831 --> 00:15:02.129
I must continue the hunt.

00:15:02.167 --> 00:15:05.534
Not without your ship
and not in this condition.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:07.595
You'll die without treatment.

00:15:07.639 --> 00:15:09.766
Let us help you.

00:15:14.279 --> 00:15:15.769
Doctor?

00:15:19.885 --> 00:15:21.113
All right...

00:15:21.153 --> 00:15:23.348
I'm going to enter
the force field now

00:15:23.388 --> 00:15:26.551
and start with a few scans
of your midsection.

00:15:26.591 --> 00:15:28.115
You should know I'm a hologram

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:30.526
and can't be bent,
spindled or mutilated

00:15:30.562 --> 00:15:32.530
so don't bother trying.

00:15:32.564 --> 00:15:35.658
Hmm.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.225
Please lie down.

00:15:40.972 --> 00:15:43.031
Or remain standing.

00:15:46.845 --> 00:15:49.143
Captain, we've detected
six more Hirogen ships.

00:15:49.181 --> 00:15:50.978
They're converging on us
from all directions.

00:15:51.016 --> 00:15:52.210
The one in Sick Bay

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:54.650
may have sent a distress call
from his vessel.

00:15:54.686 --> 00:15:56.551
How long do we have?

00:15:56.588 --> 00:15:58.112
The nearest ship
is half a light-year away...

00:15:58.156 --> 00:15:59.145
four hours at most.

00:16:00.492 --> 00:16:03.359
Tom, analyze
their approach pattern.

00:16:03.395 --> 00:16:04.862
Evade them as long as you can.

00:16:04.896 --> 00:16:06.887
Yes, ma'am.

00:16:06.932 --> 00:16:09.332
I want to buy the Doctor enough
time to treat our hunter.

00:16:09.367 --> 00:16:12.427
If I can gain his confidence,
he might call off his friends.

00:16:12.471 --> 00:16:14.871
Good old-fashioned diplomacy
could get us out of this yet.

00:16:14.906 --> 00:16:16.271
Don't count on it.

00:16:16.308 --> 00:16:17.741
From what I found
in their database,

00:16:17.776 --> 00:16:19.801
diplomacy isn't a part
of their lifestyle.

00:16:19.845 --> 00:16:21.210
They don't see us as equals.

00:16:21.246 --> 00:16:22.847
To them, we're simply game.

00:16:22.980 --> 00:16:24.345
It's time
we convince them otherwise...

00:16:24.381 --> 00:16:27.509
or like any other cornered
animal, we'll show our teeth.

00:16:27.551 --> 00:16:31.612
There's been a hull rupture
on Deck 11, Section 3.

00:16:31.655 --> 00:16:33.213
Damage is minor.

00:16:33.257 --> 00:16:35.248
It appears
a plasma conduit overloaded.

00:16:35.292 --> 00:16:38.693
Increase power to the structural
integrity field.

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:43.163
A bulkhead has collapsed
in Jefferies Tube 84.

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:44.326
Another overload?

00:16:44.368 --> 00:16:47.303
Negative.
The plasma network is stable.

00:16:47.338 --> 00:16:49.363
This wasn't caused by any
power surge or system failure.

00:16:49.406 --> 00:16:52.933
Harry, Tuvok, get to Deck 11
and check it out.

00:17:06.991 --> 00:17:08.515
This was no overload.

00:17:08.559 --> 00:17:10.117
Indeed.

00:17:11.996 --> 00:17:13.793
Commander.

00:17:23.941 --> 00:17:28.173
It's a dense mixture of DNA
and polyfluidic compounds.

00:17:28.212 --> 00:17:29.611
Tuvok to Bridge.

00:17:29.647 --> 00:17:30.477
Go ahead.

00:17:30.514 --> 00:17:32.482
We may have
an intruder on board.

00:17:32.516 --> 00:17:35.144
I'm analyzing what could be
a sample of its blood.

00:17:35.185 --> 00:17:39.212
The readings are consistent
with Species 8472.

00:17:40.591 --> 00:17:41.558
Intruder alert.

00:17:41.592 --> 00:17:42.559
Bridge to Security.

00:17:42.593 --> 00:17:44.322
Seal off Decks 10 through 12.

00:17:44.361 --> 00:17:48.127
Internal sensors
aren't detecting any intruders.

00:17:48.165 --> 00:17:50.531
The last time
we ran into this species,

00:17:50.567 --> 00:17:52.967
it was impervious
to our scanners.

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:55.630
We'll have to track it visually.

00:17:57.942 --> 00:17:59.569
How did it get
past our shields?

00:17:59.610 --> 00:18:00.770
We'll worry about that later.

00:18:00.811 --> 00:18:02.005
You have the Bridge, Commander.

00:18:02.046 --> 00:18:03.274
I'll be on Deck 11.

00:18:07.618 --> 00:18:10.280
I've erected a level-10 force
field around Engineering.

00:18:10.321 --> 00:18:11.913
Good. Set up
secondary force fields

00:18:11.956 --> 00:18:14.220
around every hatch,
Jefferies tube and conduit

00:18:14.258 --> 00:18:15.520
leading into this room.

00:18:15.559 --> 00:18:18.722
I want every one
of these consoles secured...

00:18:18.762 --> 00:18:20.195
authorized command codes only.

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:22.255
I'm going to lock down
the warp core.

00:18:22.299 --> 00:18:23.926
Ensign, realign
the dilithium matrix

00:18:24.034 --> 00:18:27.697
to a frequency of 3.69.

00:18:43.954 --> 00:18:44.943
Report.

00:18:44.989 --> 00:18:47.184
Four crew members are
wounded, two seriously.

00:18:48.926 --> 00:18:50.621
Get them to Sick Bay.

00:18:50.661 --> 00:18:53.221
Species 8472
accessed Engineering

00:18:53.263 --> 00:18:54.958
through the antimatter
injector port.

00:18:55.032 --> 00:18:57.830
Our phaser fire
was insufficient.

00:18:57.868 --> 00:19:01.031
It attacked us, then escaped
through Jefferies Tube 17-Alpha.

00:19:01.071 --> 00:19:02.868
Janeway to Tuvok.

00:19:02.906 --> 00:19:03.873
Tuvok here.

00:19:03.907 --> 00:19:05.499
The intruder
just left Engineering.

00:19:05.542 --> 00:19:06.634
Seal off the area.

00:19:06.677 --> 00:19:07.871
Understood.

00:19:07.911 --> 00:19:08.775
Secure the warp core.

00:19:08.812 --> 00:19:09.710
Yes, Captain.

00:19:09.747 --> 00:19:10.907
Seven.

00:19:17.554 --> 00:19:19.454
It would seem that the Hirogen

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:21.617
underestimated
their latest prey.

00:19:21.658 --> 00:19:23.285
You believe they were
hunting the creature.

00:19:23.327 --> 00:19:26.421
Yes. When the Borg
were fighting Species 8472,

00:19:26.463 --> 00:19:28.192
did they ever engage
in physical combat?

00:19:28.232 --> 00:19:29.563
On many occasions.

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:32.933
Can you recall anything
that might help us here?

00:19:33.003 --> 00:19:34.868
Each time they boarded
a Borg vessel,

00:19:34.905 --> 00:19:36.930
they went directly
to the central power matrix

00:19:37.007 --> 00:19:38.235
and disabled it.

00:19:38.275 --> 00:19:39.765
The creature was just
in Engineering.

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:41.937
Didn't touch any
of our power systems.

00:19:42.046 --> 00:19:43.946
It's obviously adjusted
its strategy.

00:19:44.048 --> 00:19:47.677
Species 8472 is devious
and highly intelligent.

00:19:47.718 --> 00:19:50.380
It will seek the most efficient
means of destroying us.

00:19:50.421 --> 00:19:51.683
Let's get to Sick Bay.

00:20:04.201 --> 00:20:07.500
She's going to be
just fine, Captain.

00:20:07.538 --> 00:20:09.369
Is it alone?

00:20:09.406 --> 00:20:11.465
Have you seen
any others like it?

00:20:11.508 --> 00:20:12.839
Why?

00:20:12.876 --> 00:20:15.071
Six months ago, this species
invaded our galaxy

00:20:15.112 --> 00:20:16.238
with thousands of ships.

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:17.713
We were barely able
to fight them off.

00:20:17.748 --> 00:20:19.978
Your prey could indicate
another invasion.

00:20:20.084 --> 00:20:21.984
If it does,
we're all in trouble.

00:20:22.019 --> 00:20:24.579
How many ships have you seen?

00:20:24.621 --> 00:20:27.454
Only one. Damaged.

00:20:27.491 --> 00:20:30.756
We tracked it
across 50 light-years.

00:20:30.794 --> 00:20:32.762
We thought that we had
killed the creature,

00:20:32.796 --> 00:20:35.356
but this prey is
unlike any other.

00:20:35.399 --> 00:20:37.264
It has many lives.

00:20:37.301 --> 00:20:41.567
Lower the force field
and I will finish the hunt.

00:20:41.605 --> 00:20:43.835
Your attempt to destroy
it will fail.

00:20:43.874 --> 00:20:47.401
Species 8472 is highly
resistant to all technology.

00:20:47.444 --> 00:20:50.607
All but one...
Borg nanoprobes.

00:20:50.647 --> 00:20:52.137
"Nanoprobes"?

00:20:52.182 --> 00:20:53.479
Microscopic weapons that can

00:20:53.517 --> 00:20:55.678
attack the species
on a cellular level.

00:20:55.719 --> 00:20:58.017
We've tried it before
and it worked.

00:20:58.088 --> 00:21:01.455
I'll modify the phaser rifles
to fire nanoprobe discharges.

00:21:01.492 --> 00:21:03.619
I want you to incapacitate
the creature, not kill it.

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:04.888
Can you make that modification?

00:21:04.928 --> 00:21:07.829
Yes, but it would
require additional time.

00:21:07.865 --> 00:21:10.060
We must stop it
as soon as possible.

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:11.124
She's right.

00:21:11.168 --> 00:21:13.568
Not until we know
why it returned.

00:21:13.604 --> 00:21:15.970
You will be exposing this crew
to unnecessary risk.

00:21:16.006 --> 00:21:16.973
I disagree.

00:21:17.007 --> 00:21:17.974
Captain...

00:21:18.008 --> 00:21:20.203
You have your orders, Seven.

00:21:20.244 --> 00:21:22.974
Six of your vessels will be here
in under four hours.

00:21:23.046 --> 00:21:26.538
I hope you'll let them know
that we saved your life

00:21:26.583 --> 00:21:29.484
and that we want to avoid
any further conflict

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:30.817
with your people.

00:21:30.854 --> 00:21:34.585
Let me resume the hunt,
and I will grant your request.

00:21:34.625 --> 00:21:37.458
We have enough problems
on this ship as it is

00:21:37.494 --> 00:21:38.961
without him running around.

00:21:38.996 --> 00:21:42.363
I spent six months studying
this prey's behavior.

00:21:42.399 --> 00:21:44.094
I know how to track him.

00:21:44.134 --> 00:21:49.162
Let me continue or I will have
the others destroy you.

00:21:51.808 --> 00:21:52.900
Tuvok to Janeway.

00:21:52.943 --> 00:21:54.001
Go ahead.

00:21:54.044 --> 00:21:56.308
We're holding position
in Section 94,

00:21:56.346 --> 00:21:59.611
but the creature has accessed
the environmental controls.

00:21:59.650 --> 00:22:01.948
Deck 11 is losing life support.

00:22:05.122 --> 00:22:07.682
Artificial gravity has also
been compromised.

00:22:07.724 --> 00:22:08.952
Evacuate the deck.

00:22:08.992 --> 00:22:10.289
Regroup on Deck 10.

00:22:10.327 --> 00:22:11.487
Aye, Captain.

00:22:11.528 --> 00:22:13.826
He's trying
to barricade himself.

00:22:13.864 --> 00:22:15.456
He did the same thing to us.

00:22:15.499 --> 00:22:17.126
You want to be part of the hunt?

00:22:17.167 --> 00:22:19.101
Now's your chance.

00:22:19.136 --> 00:22:21.297
He'll be under
your supervision, Commander.

00:22:21.338 --> 00:22:24.102
If he steps out of line,
shoot him.

00:22:40.924 --> 00:22:42.551
My weapon.

00:22:46.096 --> 00:22:47.688
Temperature gradient.

00:22:47.731 --> 00:22:49.665
Affirmative.

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:51.600
Atmospheric recyclers.

00:22:51.635 --> 00:22:53.694
Engaged.

00:22:55.772 --> 00:22:57.672
Is your body armor
designed to handle

00:22:57.708 --> 00:22:59.335
rapid pressure fluctuations?

00:22:59.376 --> 00:23:03.335
It can defeat
most hostile environments.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:06.508
I once tracked
a silicon-based life-form

00:23:06.550 --> 00:23:09.951
through the neutronium mantle
of a collapsed star.

00:23:10.020 --> 00:23:13.547
I once tracked a mouse
through Jefferies Tube 32.

00:23:17.594 --> 00:23:19.892
Chakotay to Tuvok.
We're ready to go.

00:23:19.930 --> 00:23:21.727
As are we.

00:23:21.765 --> 00:23:23.130
Proceed to Deck 11.

00:23:23.166 --> 00:23:24.793
Keep your com links open.

00:23:24.835 --> 00:23:28.430
Understood.
Activate the nanoprobe charges.

00:23:28.472 --> 00:23:31.373
Level five should be sufficient
to stun the creature.

00:23:43.287 --> 00:23:45.278
Depressurizing hatch.

00:23:45.322 --> 00:23:46.653
Magnetize.

00:24:51.021 --> 00:24:53.114
Maintain your position.

00:24:53.156 --> 00:24:55.522
He's here.

00:24:55.559 --> 00:24:57.891
I said maintain your position.

00:24:57.928 --> 00:24:59.395
This is my hunt.

00:24:59.429 --> 00:25:00.794
I'm at point.

00:25:00.831 --> 00:25:04.096
My knowledge of this prey
is superior to yours.

00:25:04.134 --> 00:25:05.567
But you're
on unfamiliar terrain.

00:25:05.602 --> 00:25:07.092
I know this ship.

00:25:07.137 --> 00:25:08.195
You don't.

00:25:08.238 --> 00:25:11.901
The prey will likely attack
the man at point.

00:25:13.944 --> 00:25:15.844
You would not survive.

00:25:15.879 --> 00:25:18.211
I'll take that chance.

00:25:18.248 --> 00:25:20.079
Now, fall back.

00:25:34.097 --> 00:25:35.325
No problem.

00:25:35.365 --> 00:25:37.230
I'll take up the rear.

00:26:05.095 --> 00:26:06.687
You missed.

00:26:09.833 --> 00:26:12.734
Since Species 8472
invaded the ship,

00:26:12.769 --> 00:26:15.101
you've become
increasingly agitated.

00:26:15.138 --> 00:26:17.129
They were the only species

00:26:17.174 --> 00:26:19.768
to offer true resistance
to the Borg.

00:26:19.810 --> 00:26:22.142
They destroyed
millions of drones,

00:26:22.179 --> 00:26:23.942
hundreds of our worlds.

00:26:24.047 --> 00:26:27.278
I have reason to be agitated.

00:26:39.629 --> 00:26:41.597
What is it?

00:26:41.631 --> 00:26:43.360
It's blood.

00:26:43.400 --> 00:26:45.129
The prey is wounded.

00:26:45.168 --> 00:26:48.262
This corridor ends
about 20 meters ahead.

00:26:48.305 --> 00:26:50.899
The only thing down there
is Deflector Control.

00:26:50.941 --> 00:26:52.602
It's got nowhere to run.

00:26:52.642 --> 00:26:54.974
He is not planning to run.

00:26:55.045 --> 00:26:56.706
He is waiting.

00:26:56.746 --> 00:27:00.443
He'll attempt to slip around us,
attack from behind.

00:27:01.785 --> 00:27:03.446
Chakotay to Tuvok.

00:27:03.487 --> 00:27:04.749
Tuvok here.

00:27:04.788 --> 00:27:07.586
We've cornered the intruder
in Section 59.

00:27:07.624 --> 00:27:09.489
On our way.

00:27:20.736 --> 00:27:22.101
It's hurt.

00:27:22.138 --> 00:27:24.470
This prey is resilient.

00:27:24.507 --> 00:27:27.101
He will strike
with his dying breath.

00:27:29.812 --> 00:27:32.110
We must kill him now.

00:27:32.148 --> 00:27:33.740
That may not be necessary.

00:27:35.284 --> 00:27:36.842
Hold your fire.

00:27:36.886 --> 00:27:37.978
I said lower your weapon!

00:28:13.422 --> 00:28:15.822
Mr. Neelix, I must ask you

00:28:15.858 --> 00:28:18.122
to exchange your spatula
for a phaser rifle.

00:28:18.160 --> 00:28:19.422
Sir?

00:28:19.462 --> 00:28:20.929
We have
two intruders onboard

00:28:21.030 --> 00:28:22.930
and six Hirogen vessels
on the way.

00:28:22.998 --> 00:28:24.625
I need additional
security personnel.

00:28:24.667 --> 00:28:26.601
Right away, sir.

00:28:26.635 --> 00:28:28.660
What's my assignment?

00:28:28.704 --> 00:28:31.901
Join the security detail
on Deck 10, Section 12.

00:28:31.941 --> 00:28:34.705
You'll receive
further instructions there.

00:28:34.744 --> 00:28:35.972
I'll expect tactical updates
every 20 min...

00:28:41.050 --> 00:28:42.574
Lieutenant?

00:28:42.618 --> 00:28:44.142
Are you all right?

00:28:44.186 --> 00:28:46.051
You have your orders.

00:28:48.624 --> 00:28:50.717
Report.

00:28:50.760 --> 00:28:53.354
The Hirogen's back in Sick Bay
within a force field.

00:28:53.395 --> 00:28:54.953
And Species 8472?

00:28:55.064 --> 00:28:56.463
We've established
a security perimeter.

00:28:56.499 --> 00:28:58.865
Basically, we've turned this
entire section into a brig.

00:28:58.901 --> 00:29:01.199
As an added precaution,
have B'Elanna start working

00:29:01.237 --> 00:29:02.864
on a way
to lock onto the creature,

00:29:02.905 --> 00:29:04.805
in case we have to beam it
off the ship.

00:29:04.840 --> 00:29:06.705
You mentioned it was injured.
In what way?

00:29:06.742 --> 00:29:07.902
I wish I could tell you
for certain.

00:29:07.977 --> 00:29:10.571
Its body is generating
some sort bioelectric field

00:29:10.613 --> 00:29:11.807
making it impossible to scan,

00:29:11.847 --> 00:29:14.145
so I could only make
a visual diagnosis.

00:29:14.183 --> 00:29:16.276
It's conscious but immobile.

00:29:16.318 --> 00:29:18.479
Its epidermis displays
any number of injuries...

00:29:18.521 --> 00:29:20.489
punctures, energy burns...

00:29:20.523 --> 00:29:23.788
and its demeanor is that
of a wounded animal.

00:29:23.826 --> 00:29:26.158
The Hirogen said they'd been
chasing it for several months.

00:29:26.195 --> 00:29:27.253
Is there anything you can do?

00:29:27.296 --> 00:29:29.161
I don't know enough
about its physiology

00:29:29.198 --> 00:29:30.460
to treat the surface wounds,

00:29:30.499 --> 00:29:31.932
let alone any internal damage.

00:29:31.967 --> 00:29:33.832
Frankly, I'm at a loss.

00:29:35.371 --> 00:29:36.929
Captain, just
before we cornered it,

00:29:37.006 --> 00:29:40.942
Species 8472 accessed deflector
control from this panel.

00:29:41.010 --> 00:29:43.103
I've analyzed
the transmission protocols.

00:29:43.145 --> 00:29:45.943
It was attempting to open
a singularity into its realm,

00:29:45.981 --> 00:29:47.073
but it failed.

00:29:47.116 --> 00:29:49.448
It was trying to get home.

00:29:49.485 --> 00:29:51.282
That's what it looks like.

00:30:01.630 --> 00:30:03.257
Tuvok?

00:30:03.299 --> 00:30:07.793
The creature initiated
telepathic contact with me.

00:30:08.838 --> 00:30:10.567
What's it saying?

00:30:17.346 --> 00:30:20.941
Lts ship was damaged during
the conflict with the Borg.

00:30:20.983 --> 00:30:24.885
When the other members
of its species retreated

00:30:24.920 --> 00:30:26.683
into fluidic space...

00:30:26.722 --> 00:30:28.314
it was left behind.

00:30:32.561 --> 00:30:35.826
It has been trapped in the
Delta Quadrant ever since...

00:30:35.865 --> 00:30:38.265
alone...

00:30:38.300 --> 00:30:41.167
pursued
by Hirogen hunting parties.

00:30:41.203 --> 00:30:45.572
It has no desire
for further conflict.

00:30:45.608 --> 00:30:49.135
It only wants to return
to its domain.

00:30:49.178 --> 00:30:51.772
It is dying, Captain.

00:30:59.288 --> 00:31:02.189
You have nothing
to be afraid of.

00:31:04.193 --> 00:31:06.787
We're going to help you
get back to your realm.

00:31:06.829 --> 00:31:08.888
Does it understand?

00:31:08.931 --> 00:31:10.865
It does.

00:31:10.900 --> 00:31:14.859
It will take time
to open a singularity,

00:31:14.904 --> 00:31:18.863
and we have no way
of treating your injuries,

00:31:18.908 --> 00:31:21.706
but if there's anything
you can tell us about your...

00:31:28.684 --> 00:31:31.209
It has lost consciousness.

00:31:31.253 --> 00:31:34.154
Our telepathic link
has been severed.

00:31:44.300 --> 00:31:46.928
Where is my prey?

00:31:46.969 --> 00:31:49.995
Lying at the end of a corridor
on Deck 11...

00:31:50.072 --> 00:31:51.972
nearly dead thanks to you.

00:31:52.007 --> 00:31:53.372
Take me to it.

00:31:53.409 --> 00:31:54.433
No.

00:31:54.476 --> 00:31:56.603
Take me to it!

00:31:56.645 --> 00:31:59.341
In less than three hours,
your ships will arrive.

00:31:59.381 --> 00:32:04.944
By that time, Species 8472
will no longer be on Voyager.

00:32:04.987 --> 00:32:06.318
What do you mean?

00:32:06.355 --> 00:32:08.619
I'm sending it back
where it came from.

00:32:08.657 --> 00:32:14.425
Surrender the creature to me
and you will not be harmed.

00:32:14.463 --> 00:32:16.397
This isn't a hunt;
it's a slaughter.

00:32:16.432 --> 00:32:18.127
And I'm calling it off
right now.

00:32:18.167 --> 00:32:22.934
We will not be denied our prey.

00:32:22.972 --> 00:32:26.066
Give us the creature...

00:32:27.810 --> 00:32:31.871
or your crew
will take its place.

00:32:33.549 --> 00:32:35.073
Tuvok?

00:32:44.827 --> 00:32:46.852
Have Seven of Nine
report to my ready room.

00:32:46.895 --> 00:32:48.123
You intend to ask her

00:32:48.163 --> 00:32:50.290
to open a rift
into 8472's realm.

00:32:50.332 --> 00:32:52.391
She's the only one
on board who knows how.

00:32:52.434 --> 00:32:53.867
Given her feelings
toward the species,

00:32:53.902 --> 00:32:55.335
she may not want to cooperate.

00:32:55.371 --> 00:32:56.360
We'll see.

00:33:01.944 --> 00:33:04.208
You wish to see me, Captain?

00:33:04.246 --> 00:33:08.080
I've made a decision
about Species 8472.

00:33:08.117 --> 00:33:10.950
I'm going to return it
to fluidic space.

00:33:10.986 --> 00:33:14.387
In order to do that, I need you
to open a quantum singularity.

00:33:14.423 --> 00:33:17.221
I don't believe that is
a prudent course of action.

00:33:17.259 --> 00:33:18.556
I realize it may be

00:33:18.594 --> 00:33:21.358
difficult for you to help
save this creature's life,

00:33:21.397 --> 00:33:24.958
but part of becoming human
is learning to have compassion

00:33:25.034 --> 00:33:26.831
for those who are suffering,

00:33:26.869 --> 00:33:30.168
even when they're
your bitter enemies.

00:33:31.006 --> 00:33:31.995
Why?

00:33:33.675 --> 00:33:36.974
I remember
when I was a Lieutenant.

00:33:37.079 --> 00:33:39.980
It was during
a Cardassian border conflict.

00:33:40.049 --> 00:33:41.949
My away team was cut off

00:33:41.984 --> 00:33:44.418
while we were defending
a Federation outpost.

00:33:44.453 --> 00:33:45.818
We'd been exchanging
phaser fire

00:33:45.854 --> 00:33:48.755
with a group of Cardassians
for about three days...

00:33:48.791 --> 00:33:50.622
a stalemate.

00:33:52.461 --> 00:33:57.091
One night, during
a break in the fighting...

00:33:57.132 --> 00:34:00.795
we could hear
this low moaning sound

00:34:00.836 --> 00:34:02.701
coming from somewhere
in the brush.

00:34:02.738 --> 00:34:05.172
We knew that none
of our people were out there,

00:34:05.207 --> 00:34:07.107
so it had to be
a wounded Cardassian.

00:34:07.142 --> 00:34:09.667
Well, you have to understand...

00:34:09.711 --> 00:34:12.373
we'd been killing each other
for weeks on this planet.

00:34:12.414 --> 00:34:13.904
It was brutal.

00:34:16.351 --> 00:34:18.410
But our commanding officer
decided...

00:34:20.456 --> 00:34:22.447
that we couldn't just sit there

00:34:22.491 --> 00:34:24.686
and listen
to that poor man suffer.

00:34:24.726 --> 00:34:29.288
So he ordered me
and an Ensign...

00:34:30.866 --> 00:34:32.356
to crawl out there

00:34:32.401 --> 00:34:34.801
and bring that Cardassian
back to our camp.

00:34:34.837 --> 00:34:36.065
I thought he was crazy.

00:34:36.105 --> 00:34:38.073
He was risking our lives
for someone

00:34:38.107 --> 00:34:40.473
who would have shot us
without hesitation.

00:34:42.311 --> 00:34:43.403
But we did it...

00:34:45.681 --> 00:34:47.410
and the Cardassian lived.

00:34:47.449 --> 00:34:50.282
Three days later,
we secured the outpost.

00:34:50.319 --> 00:34:51.684
It was a major victory.

00:34:51.720 --> 00:34:54.587
We were all decorated
by Starfleet Command,

00:34:54.623 --> 00:34:57.285
but in retrospect...

00:34:57.326 --> 00:34:59.590
the thing I'm most proud of

00:34:59.628 --> 00:35:02.620
was the night we saved
that man's life.

00:35:04.833 --> 00:35:06.323
Explain.

00:35:13.375 --> 00:35:15.866
A single act of compassion

00:35:15.911 --> 00:35:19.039
can put you in touch
with your own humanity.

00:35:19.081 --> 00:35:23.450
You are trying to justify
your present decision.

00:35:23.485 --> 00:35:24.611
No.

00:35:24.653 --> 00:35:28.612
I'm trying to help you see
this as an opportunity to grow.

00:35:28.657 --> 00:35:31.490
I know you don't want
to do it, Seven,

00:35:31.527 --> 00:35:33.825
but I'm telling you
as your Captain

00:35:33.862 --> 00:35:36.956
and as your friend,
you won't regret it.

00:35:38.901 --> 00:35:40.266
No.

00:35:40.302 --> 00:35:42.964
Your decision is
tactically unsound.

00:35:43.005 --> 00:35:44.973
We will be surrounded
by Hirogen ships

00:35:45.040 --> 00:35:46.439
in approximately two hours.

00:35:46.475 --> 00:35:47.965
If we do not surrender
the creature,

00:35:48.043 --> 00:35:50.170
they will destroy us.

00:35:50.212 --> 00:35:52.942
A lesson in compassion
will do me little good

00:35:52.981 --> 00:35:54.141
if I am dead.

00:35:54.183 --> 00:35:57.311
It is wrong to sacrifice
another being

00:35:57.352 --> 00:35:59.149
to save our own lives.

00:35:59.188 --> 00:36:00.951
I have observed that
you have been willing

00:36:00.989 --> 00:36:03.457
to sacrifice your own life
to save the lives of your crew.

00:36:03.492 --> 00:36:04.925
Yes, but that's different.

00:36:04.993 --> 00:36:06.051
That was my choice.

00:36:06.094 --> 00:36:08.426
This creature
does not have a choice.

00:36:09.264 --> 00:36:11.755
It invaded our ship,

00:36:11.800 --> 00:36:13.927
put our lives at risk
to save its own.

00:36:14.002 --> 00:36:17.335
In my view, it has already
forfeited its freedom.

00:36:18.340 --> 00:36:19.864
I'm giving you an order.

00:36:19.908 --> 00:36:21.205
Report to Deflector Control

00:36:21.243 --> 00:36:23.905
and begin working
on creating a singularity.

00:36:23.946 --> 00:36:26.107
I will not comply.

00:36:27.349 --> 00:36:29.408
I have agreed
to remain on Voyager.

00:36:29.451 --> 00:36:32.579
I have agreed to function
as a member of your crew,

00:36:32.621 --> 00:36:34.282
but I will not be a willing

00:36:34.323 --> 00:36:36.257
participant
in my own destruction

00:36:36.291 --> 00:36:38.418
or the destruction of this ship.

00:36:39.628 --> 00:36:41.255
Objection noted.

00:36:41.296 --> 00:36:42.524
We'll do this without you.

00:36:43.632 --> 00:36:45.065
You will fail.

00:36:45.100 --> 00:36:47.762
And you have just
crossed the line.

00:36:47.803 --> 00:36:48.770
End of debate.

00:36:48.804 --> 00:36:49.930
Report to the cargo bay

00:36:49.972 --> 00:36:51.769
and remain there
until this is over.

00:36:51.807 --> 00:36:53.968
Is that understood?

00:37:13.328 --> 00:37:15.193
Shields down to 84 percent.

00:37:15.230 --> 00:37:16.322
Return fire.

00:37:16.365 --> 00:37:19.857
Three more ships are closing
from port and starboard.

00:37:19.901 --> 00:37:21.766
All escape trajectories
have been cut off.

00:37:21.803 --> 00:37:24.533
Our weapons are having little
effect on their hull plating.

00:37:24.573 --> 00:37:27.337
I'm scanning for weaknesses
in the molecular structure.

00:37:34.950 --> 00:37:36.247
Shields at 79 percent.

00:37:36.285 --> 00:37:37.252
They are hailing us.

00:37:37.286 --> 00:37:39.186
Better late than never.

00:37:39.221 --> 00:37:42.281
Open a channel.

00:37:42.324 --> 00:37:44.952
You've taken our prey
and one of our hunters.

00:37:45.027 --> 00:37:46.756
Surrender them.

00:37:46.795 --> 00:37:49.923
Call off your attack
and we'll return your crewman.

00:37:49.965 --> 00:37:53.457
As for your prey,
it's under our protection now.

00:37:53.502 --> 00:37:55.197
It belongs to us.

00:37:55.237 --> 00:37:57.671
It belongs to no one.

00:37:57.706 --> 00:37:59.298
Now, order your ships
to withdraw

00:37:59.341 --> 00:38:00.774
and this can end peacefully.

00:38:04.578 --> 00:38:06.512
All vessels are firing.

00:38:06.546 --> 00:38:08.571
Any luck finding
a crack in their armor?

00:38:08.615 --> 00:38:09.604
Not yet.

00:38:17.357 --> 00:38:18.688
Doctor to Bridge.

00:38:18.725 --> 00:38:21.558
Species 8472
appears to be regenerating.

00:38:23.063 --> 00:38:24.462
I'm no exobiologist,

00:38:24.497 --> 00:38:27.295
but I'd say this fellow
is becoming highly agitated.

00:38:27.334 --> 00:38:29.495
It could be sensing
the Hirogen attack.

00:38:29.536 --> 00:38:31.060
Doctor, can you sedate it?

00:38:31.104 --> 00:38:32.093
I believe so,

00:38:32.138 --> 00:38:34.197
but I'll need another dose
of Borg nanoprobes.

00:38:34.241 --> 00:38:36.675
Stand by.

00:38:36.710 --> 00:38:38.143
Bridge to Seven of Nine.

00:38:38.178 --> 00:38:39.805
Yes.

00:38:39.846 --> 00:38:43.145
Report to Deck 11 immediately
with a supply of nanoprobes.

00:38:43.183 --> 00:38:44.582
Understood.

00:38:49.623 --> 00:38:51.181
B'Elanna, how's it going
down there?

00:38:51.224 --> 00:38:52.714
Transporters are ready.

00:38:52.759 --> 00:38:55.091
I can establish a lock
on the creature at any time,

00:38:55.128 --> 00:38:57.688
but I still haven't duplicated
the deflector protocols

00:38:57.731 --> 00:38:59.323
to open a singularity.

00:38:59.366 --> 00:39:00.230
How long?

00:39:00.267 --> 00:39:03.759
I need another hour...
maybe two.

00:39:03.803 --> 00:39:05.896
Captain, we can outmaneuver
the Hirogen ships

00:39:05.939 --> 00:39:07.907
for a few more minutes,
but beyond that...

00:39:07.941 --> 00:39:10.569
Direct hit
to the EPS manifold!

00:39:10.610 --> 00:39:11.599
Main power just went down!

00:39:11.645 --> 00:39:14.239
Force fields on all decks
are off-line.

00:39:14.281 --> 00:39:15.714
Switch to auxiliary power.

00:39:16.883 --> 00:39:18.043
Done. Force fields
have been restored,

00:39:18.084 --> 00:39:20.552
but I don't know
how long they'll hold.

00:39:20.587 --> 00:39:22.919
Bridge to Doctor.
Report.

00:39:22.956 --> 00:39:24.184
It's all right, Captain.

00:39:24.224 --> 00:39:25.555
The creature is contained.

00:39:25.592 --> 00:39:26.923
Bridge to Sick Bay.

00:39:28.261 --> 00:39:30.821
Security respond.

00:39:38.738 --> 00:39:40.899
Security, dispatch teams
to Deck 5.

00:39:40.941 --> 00:39:43.205
The Hirogen may be loose.

00:39:43.243 --> 00:39:45.973
Direct hit
to our port nacelle.

00:39:47.747 --> 00:39:49.908
Now, they've taken out
our starboard nacelle.

00:39:49.950 --> 00:39:50.939
They've crippled us.

00:39:50.984 --> 00:39:53.282
Tuvok, divert warp power
to the phaser banks.

00:39:53.320 --> 00:39:55.982
Maybe that'll help us
penetrate their hull plating.

00:40:01.094 --> 00:40:02.061
The nanoprobes?

00:40:02.095 --> 00:40:03.062
Armed and ready.

00:40:03.096 --> 00:40:04.927
Not a moment too soon.

00:40:11.438 --> 00:40:13.065
Give me the prey.

00:40:13.106 --> 00:40:16.633
Lower your weapon
or I will destroy you.

00:40:19.512 --> 00:40:21.605
I don't think you will.

00:40:21.648 --> 00:40:24.344
You want me to destroy
this creature.

00:40:24.384 --> 00:40:28.582
I saw it on your face
earlier in the medical bay.

00:40:28.621 --> 00:40:31.249
It's a look I've seen
a thousand times.

00:40:31.291 --> 00:40:34.749
Stand aside.

00:40:52.979 --> 00:40:54.606
What are you doing?

00:40:56.082 --> 00:40:58.607
Captain, someone's accessing
the transporter system

00:40:58.651 --> 00:40:59.618
from Deck 5.

00:40:59.652 --> 00:41:00.619
Lock them out.

00:41:00.653 --> 00:41:01.551
I can't.

00:41:01.588 --> 00:41:03.055
They're overriding
my commands...

00:41:03.089 --> 00:41:05.182
with Borg encryption codes.

00:41:17.337 --> 00:41:18.964
Report, Mr. Kim.

00:41:19.005 --> 00:41:20.973
8472 and the Hirogen...

00:41:21.007 --> 00:41:22.975
they've been beamed to one
of the attacking ships.

00:41:23.009 --> 00:41:25.637
All six vessels are moving away
at high warp.

00:41:25.678 --> 00:41:27.646
Tom, can we pursue?

00:41:28.948 --> 00:41:30.313
I'm sorry, Captain.

00:41:30.350 --> 00:41:32.147
Warp engines are still off-line.

00:41:34.054 --> 00:41:36.454
Resume our previous course.

00:41:36.489 --> 00:41:37.683
Full impulse.

00:41:41.761 --> 00:41:43.251
Seven of Nine?

00:41:46.499 --> 00:41:48.160
Seven of Nine.

00:41:49.903 --> 00:41:54.636
Captain's Log, Stardate 51652.3.

00:41:54.674 --> 00:41:55.936
It's been 12 hours

00:41:55.975 --> 00:41:58.967
and our sensors show no sign
of any Hirogen vessels,

00:41:59.012 --> 00:42:01.446
but their people are scattered
throughout this region

00:42:01.481 --> 00:42:02.709
and something tells me

00:42:02.749 --> 00:42:05.115
that the "hunt" for Voyager
is far from over.

00:42:41.855 --> 00:42:42.913
Captain.

00:42:42.956 --> 00:42:44.514
Step down, please.

00:42:49.195 --> 00:42:52.426
Seven, you disobeyed
my direct orders

00:42:52.465 --> 00:42:54.296
and as a result,

00:42:54.334 --> 00:42:56.996
you condemned a sentient
being to its death.

00:42:57.070 --> 00:43:00.301
By doing so, I also diverted
the Hirogen attack,

00:43:00.340 --> 00:43:01.932
an attack which
would have destroyed us.

00:43:02.008 --> 00:43:03.032
Maybe not.

00:43:03.076 --> 00:43:05.772
In any case, the decision
wasn't yours to make.

00:43:05.812 --> 00:43:07.677
The creature broke
through the force field.

00:43:07.714 --> 00:43:08.681
I had no choice.

00:43:08.715 --> 00:43:10.842
I didn't come here
to debate your decision.

00:43:10.884 --> 00:43:13.546
I came here to inform you
of the consequences.

00:43:13.586 --> 00:43:15.952
When you first came to Voyager,

00:43:16.055 --> 00:43:17.852
I decided to grant you
the same liberties

00:43:17.891 --> 00:43:19.825
and freedoms of any crew member

00:43:19.859 --> 00:43:22.453
because I wanted you to
be a part of this family.

00:43:22.495 --> 00:43:25.953
And I've been willing
to accommodate your...

00:43:25.999 --> 00:43:28.092
unique way of doing things...

00:43:28.134 --> 00:43:30.625
even when you rubbed
somebody the wrong way

00:43:30.670 --> 00:43:32.262
or violated protocol.

00:43:32.305 --> 00:43:34.967
But this time,
I can't accommodate you.

00:43:35.008 --> 00:43:39.468
From this point forward, you
will no longer have access

00:43:39.512 --> 00:43:42.208
to any primary systems
on this ship...

00:43:42.248 --> 00:43:44.876
not without my direct
authorization.

00:43:44.918 --> 00:43:48.979
If you attempt to circumvent me,
I'll throw you in the brig.

00:43:49.088 --> 00:43:50.350
I still need your expertise

00:43:50.390 --> 00:43:52.381
in the Astrometrics Lab
if you're willing.

00:43:52.425 --> 00:43:55.394
If not, you can spend your time
here in the cargo bay.

00:43:55.428 --> 00:43:57.362
Is that understood?

00:43:59.232 --> 00:44:00.665
Yes.

00:44:04.304 --> 00:44:06.272
It is puzzling.

00:44:06.306 --> 00:44:07.398
What's that?

00:44:09.075 --> 00:44:11.600
You made me into an individual.

00:44:11.644 --> 00:44:13.509
You encouraged me
to stop thinking

00:44:13.546 --> 00:44:15.309
like a member of the collective,

00:44:15.348 --> 00:44:19.250
to cultivate my independence
and my humanity.

00:44:19.285 --> 00:44:22.721
But when I try to assert that
independence, I am punished.

00:44:22.755 --> 00:44:25.849
Individuality has its limits...

00:44:25.892 --> 00:44:29.350
especially on a starship where
there's a command structure.

00:44:33.166 --> 00:44:34.963
I believe
that you are punishing me

00:44:35.068 --> 00:44:37.434
because I do not think
the way that you do,

00:44:37.470 --> 00:44:41.736
because I am not becoming
more like you.

00:44:41.774 --> 00:44:43.969
You claim to respect
my individuality,

00:44:44.077 --> 00:44:47.569
but in fact,
you are frightened by it.

00:44:49.782 --> 00:44:51.807
As you were.
